# 0160: group move destinations follow gamemd's MegaMission distribution (FUN_0064CDA0).
#
# Until now a group order took the nearest free cells to the click (rings out from the goal) and gave
# each to the nearest unit. Retail does not spread a selection in rings. Per the reverse-engineered
# description in github.com/YuriPlanet/vera20k (src/sim/movement/group_destination.rs, read only):
#   - the unit nearest the group's 3-D centroid (lepton coordinates) is the anchor; a tie keeps the
#     highest index (the loop scans down from the last member);
#   - members are sorted by 3-D distance from the anchor; the nearest takes the clicked cell;
#   - every other member probes up to six cells from the click centre along its own direction
#     (its navigation cell minus the anchor's cell, normalised, float arithmetic, truncated to a
#     cell): not in the playfield stops the probe, a cell outside the click's zone is "bad" and
#     skipped, an already reserved cell becomes the fallback and the probe goes on, a height-band
#     failure stops, Can_Enter_Cell >= 4 (except 6) is "bad", and the first usable cell is taken
#     unless a bad cell was seen before it (then the saved fallback, the click cell or the last
#     reserved one, is kept: retail runs a zone estimate there and ignores its result);
#   - members standing in one cell share the destination of the first of them that was assigned
#     (this is how a squad ends up sharing a cell: there is no "three infantry" rule).
# A column therefore stays a column and a flank stays on its side, where the rings put the nearest
# unit in whatever slot was left. Where retail's units sort a shared cell out on arrival (scatter),
# vehicles here take the nearest free cell to the choice and infantry beyond the three spots of a
# cell spill through assign_infantry_formation, so nobody is sent to a cell that cannot hold them.
# Air groups keep the old spread.
# Measured with `--probe-move` PROBE_SCEN=1 (xmp31s2, 12 Rhino): settled 561 -> 547 frames, blocked
# unit frames 495 -> 458; 10 Apocalypse + 10 GI 1101 -> 1074 frames, 2979 -> 2854 blocked frames.
# (The probe spawns every unit in one 3x3 blob, so a unit ringed in by its friends is scattered by
# retail's own rule and ends near its start in either version.)

